    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n80899" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπειρᾰ</span></b> , ἡ, rare fem.
		of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπων</span> (formed on analogy of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πίειρα</span>, fem. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πίων</span>), used of women, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>mellow, ripe</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ταῖς
				πεπείραις</span> (v.l. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οις</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				896
			</span></i> ; <i>over-ripe, passée</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. γίνομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anacr.
					87
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπειρα: γραῖα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of things, <i>soft,
			pulpy</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν σάρκα πέπειραν ποιεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>VC</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			 (v.l. - <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>) :
			metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργὴ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					728
				</span></i>
			.</div>
